# Kaizen on errors (cxado core)

When any error appears — test failure, CI red, build break — **stop guessing**. Use metacognition before the next change.

## Trigger

- Verify command exits non-zero.
- Same failure twice after a fix.
- Cannot explain why in one sentence.

## Method: 5 Whys

Stop at a controllable root cause (code, config, plan gap).

```markdown
## 5 Whys — <title>
**Symptom:** <command, log>
**Root cause:** <one sentence>
**Gemba:** <repro command>
```

## Gemba Kaizen workflow

1. Reproduce with the exact failing command.
2. Smallest fix at the true failure point.
3. Re-run failing check, then layer regression.
4. Kaizen note in PR: symptom → cause → fix → guard.

Bugfix PRs are gated on this at critic review — see the Kaizen checklist in [core-agent-critic.mdc](core-agent-critic.mdc)'s verdict template.
